@unit
@unit.datafactory
Feature: Data factory transactions
  # The files in resources/data_factory are generated by data-factory/generate.sh using go-algorand itself,
  # so they are the reference encoding for every transaction type. Do not edit them by hand.
  #
  # Each transaction file contains:
  #   id        - the transaction ID
  #   txnBlob   - base64 msgpack of the unsigned transaction
  #   stxnBlob  - base64 msgpack of the signed transaction
  #   stxn      - JSON view of stxnBlob (informational)
  #   signer    - the keys/program needed to produce stxnBlob from txnBlob (empty for stateProof)
  #
  # The group file (txGroup) contains txns (names of the individual files the group was built from),
  # txnBlobs, stxnBlobs, groupID and a signer that signed every transaction in the group.
  #
  # The signer object determines how the transaction is signed. Each ed25519 key is a 64-byte private key
  # (32-byte seed followed by 32-byte public key) under "SK", with its public key under "SignatureVerifier".
  #   singleSigner only          - ed25519 signature of the transaction (sig)
  #   msigSigners only           - multisig account built from msigVersion, msigThreshold and the signers'
  #                                public keys in order; the first msigThreshold signers sign the
  #                                transaction (msig)
  #   sksigSigner only           - salted-key signature (SKsig) of the transaction (pqsig)
  #   lsig only                  - escrow logic signature: the program with no signature (lsig.l)
  #   lsig and singleSigner      - logic signature delegated by singleSigner (lsig.l, lsig.sig)
  #   lsig and msigSigners       - logic signature delegated by the multisig account, the first
  #                                msigThreshold signers sign "MsigProgram" || multisig address || program
  #                                (lsig.l, lsig.lmsig)
  #
  # A multisig lists a subsig for every signer, in order. Signers beyond msigThreshold do not sign, so their
  # subsig contains only the public key (pk) with no signature (s).
  #   lsig and sksigSigner       - logic signature delegated by the salted-address account, which signs
  #                                "PQProgram" || salted address || program (lsig.l, lsig.pqsig)
  #
  # sksigSigner holds the signature scheme tag ("scheme") and its key pair ("pk", "sk"). SKsig files are named
  # <file>_<scheme>, and their scenarios list the scheme alongside the file:
  #   f1 - Falcon-1024. go-algorand signs with a deterministic Falcon profile, so signatures are reproducible.
  # An SKsig is encoded under the pqsig key and contains the scheme (sch), the address salt (slt), the public
  # key (pk) and the signature (sig). The salted address is SHA-512/256("PQA" || scheme || salt || pk), where
  # salt is the lowest value in 0..255 whose address is not an Edwards25519 curve point.
  #
  # lsigArgs, when present, are set as the logic signature's args (lsig.arg). Args are not signed.
  #
  # appCallWithAccess names its resources in the access list (al) instead of the foreign arrays. It contains
  # one of every ResourceRef kind: address (d), asset (s), app (p), holding (h), locals (l) and box (b), plus an
  # empty reference ({}) that only bumps the box quota. h, l and b refer to earlier entries by 1-based index into
  # al, where 0 means the sender (h.d, l.d) or the current app (l.p, b.i), and zero indices are omitted.
  #
  # rekeyedSender, when present, is the transaction sender, an account rekeyed to the signer. The signed
  # transaction additionally sets sgnr (auth address) to the signer's own address (for an escrow lsig, the
  # program's address).

  @unit.datafactory.msgpack
  Scenario Outline: Msgpack round trip (<file>)
    Given data factory transaction "<file>" loaded from "data_factory"
    When I decode the data factory txnBlob as a transaction
    Then encoding the transaction should equal the data factory txnBlob
    When I decode the data factory stxnBlob as a signed transaction
    Then encoding the signed transaction should equal the data factory stxnBlob

    Examples:
      | file                            |
      | simplePayment                   |
      | paymentWithAmount               |
      | largeNotePayment                |
      | closePayment                    |
      | leasePayment                    |
      | rekeyPayment                    |
      | simpleAssetTransfer             |
      | optInAssetTransfer              |
      | assetClawback                   |
      | assetCloseOut                   |
      | appCreate                       |
      | appUpdate                       |
      | appResize                       |
      | appDelete                       |
      | appCall                         |
      | appCallWithAccess               |
      | appCallWithForeignRefs          |
      | appOptIn                        |
      | appCloseOut                     |
      | appClearState                   |
      | assetCreate                     |
      | assetDestroy                    |
      | assetConfig                     |
      | onlineKeyRegistration           |
      | offlineKeyRegistration          |
      | nonParticipationKeyRegistration |
      | assetFreeze                     |
      | assetUnfreeze                   |
      | heartbeat                       |
      | msigPayment                     |
      | lsigPayment                     |
      | singleDelegatedPayment          |
      | msigDelegatedPayment            |
      | rekeyedPayment                  |
      | rekeyedDelegatedPayment         |
      | rekeyedMsigPayment              |
      | rekeyedLsigPayment              |
      | rekeyedMsigDelegatedPayment     |
      | stateProof                      |

